course: dictionary
lesson: 7488
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: The word possible means it can happen or it can be done. If something cannot happen, it is impossible, the opposite of possible. «Is it possible to be in two places at once?» No, that is impossible.
explain: Possible often appears in phrases. «As soon as possible» means as soon as you can. «If possible» means if you can manage it. To check, swap in the meaning: «as soon as you can» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: In maths, possible is used for counting what could happen. «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes, from 0000 to 9999.» Possible here means every code that can exist. Look at the words around it to find the meaning.
fact: Possible means it can happen or it can be done.
fact: Impossible is the opposite: it cannot happen or be done.
fact: «As soon as possible» means as soon as you can.
fact: «The best possible» means the best there can be.
fact: In maths, «how many are possible» means how many things could happen.
exercise: «A 4-digit PIN has 10,000 possible codes.» What does possible mean here? | Codes that are very long | Codes that have been lost | *Codes that can exist
exercise: Ollie lost his gift card in the worst way possible. What does «the worst way possible» mean? | Only a little bit bad | A way that could never happen | *The worst there can be
exercise: Mum says, «Ring me as soon as possible.» What does she mean? | Ring me when you are not busy | Ring me at midnight | *Ring me as soon as you can
test: «Children sit in the back seat where possible.» What does «where possible» mean? | Where it is impossible | Only in the front | Never | *Where they can manage it
test: Which word is the opposite of possible? | Easy | *Impossible | Likely | Helpful
exam: «Stings should be scraped out as soon as possible.» What does «as soon as possible» mean? | Never, because it is dangerous | *As quickly as you can | Slowly and carefully, after a long wait | Only if there is time later
